   "titulo": "Perfect future",
   "texto": [
    "**Vil have + participio** states that something will be finished at a future time: **Om en uge vil hun have afsluttet projektet.** = In a week the project will be completed. With verbs that make up the perfect with **være**, that auxiliary is also maintained: **Om en uge vil hun være kommet hjem.**",
    "**ville have/være + participio** is used on a conditional basis, according to the verb assistant."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Perfect parole",
   "texto": [
    "With **ville have** + participle you talk about something that would have happened: **Hun ville have afsluttet projektet.** = The project would have finished. Remember lesson 070: **ville** gives the meaning of «I would have» or «querría»."
   ]
